/T (Access to adequate housing and basic services is an essential part of protecting refugees and displaced communities. People forced to leave their homes may depend on temporary shelters, camps, reception centers, or host communities. In situations of prolonged displacement, inadequate housing can expose people to health risks, extreme weather, overcrowding, and limited access to essential resources. Access to clean water, sanitation, healthcare, education, energy, and food is also necessary for maintaining safe and dignified living conditions.)
